{% comment %}
  Membership or buy once — the two-way offer, merchandised.

  The simple offer block puts one plan beside a one-time purchase and prices
  both. This one sells the plan: the join price and the renewal price both
  stated, a rate per serving on each card, and the gifts that come with the
  membership shown as a panel inside the card rather than named in a line of
  copy. The choice it presents is the same; what surrounds it is the argument.

  Everything priced is read from the product. The block is told which plan to
  sell and nothing else — the join price, the strike-through, the renewal and
  both per-serving rates all come off the selected variant's own allocation, so
  a template shared across products stays right on each of them and a price
  change in Shopify lands here without an edit.

  The renewal line only appears when the plan actually has a second price
  adjustment. A plan that discounts every delivery equally has no "then" to
  state, and printing one would say the price changes when it does not.

  Gifts are typed. They are merchandising, not catalogue data: what ships with
  order 2 of a membership is not something the product knows.

  Replaces both simple_offer and onetime. It emits the same data-cwc-offer and
  data-cwc-onetime attributes those do, so the sticky bar, the price refresh and
  the add-to-cart treat it as the cards they already know — and for that same
  reason it cannot sit beside them: the script binds one one-time control per
  section, and a second would be left dead.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the member_offer block.
  - product {Object} - product being sold.
  - current_variant {Object} - variant whose allocation is priced.
  - section_id {String} - scopes the radio group name to this section.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-member-offer__block',
    block: block,
    product: product,
    current_variant: current_variant,
    section_id: section.id
  %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    The id as typed. A merchant copying from the Shopify admin can land on a
    bare number or on a gid:// URL, and the trailing segment is the number in
    both, so the last path part is taken rather than asking for a format.
  endcomment
  assign wanted_plan = block.settings.selling_plan_id | strip | split: '/' | last | strip | plus: 0

  assign has_plan = false
  assign plan_id = 0
  assign plan_price = 0
  assign plan_compare = 0
  assign plan_percent = 0
  assign plan_recurring = 0
  assign recurring_percent = 0

  for allocation in current_variant.selling_plan_allocations
    if allocation.selling_plan.id == wanted_plan
      assign has_plan = true
      assign plan_id = allocation.selling_plan.id
      assign plan_price = allocation.price
      assign plan_compare = allocation.compare_at_price | default: 0

      comment
        Each adjustment in its own right: the first is what it costs to join,
        the second what it costs to stay. Taken from the plan rather than
        derived from the prices, because the allocation price is already
        rounded to the cent and dividing it back out turns 30% into 29%.
      endcomment
      for adjustment in allocation.selling_plan.price_adjustments
        if forloop.index == 1 and adjustment.value_type == 'percentage'
          assign plan_percent = adjustment.value
        endif

        if forloop.index == 2
          case adjustment.value_type
            when 'percentage'
              assign recurring_percent = adjustment.value
              assign recurring_off = current_variant.price | times: adjustment.value | divided_by: 100.0 | round
              assign plan_recurring = current_variant.price | minus: recurring_off
            when 'fixed_amount'
              assign plan_recurring = current_variant.price | minus: adjustment.value
            when 'price'
              assign plan_recurring = adjustment.value
          endcase
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Servings for this variant, worked out the same way the section works them
    out for the payload — the size value's leading number times what a unit is
    worth, falling back to the typed count. Repeated rather than shared because
    a snippet cannot reach the section's variables, and a rate that disagreed
    with the one the script writes on the next click would be worse.
  endcomment
  assign servings = block.settings.servings_per_order | default: 0
  assign servings_option = block.settings.servings_option | strip | downcase
  assign servings_per_unit = block.settings.servings_per_unit | default: 0

  if servings_option != blank and servings_per_unit > 0
    assign servings_position = 0
    for product_option in product.options_with_values
      assign this_option_name = product_option.name | strip | downcase
      if this_option_name == servings_option
        assign servings_position = product_option.position
      endif
    endfor

    if servings_position > 0
      assign servings_key = 'option' | append: servings_position
      assign servings_value = current_variant[servings_key]
      assign servings_units = servings_value | split: ' ' | first | split: '-' | first | plus: 0
      if servings_units > 0
        assign servings = servings_units | times: servings_per_unit
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign member_serving = ''
  assign onetime_serving = ''
  if servings > 0
    if has_plan
      assign member_serving = plan_price | times: 1.0 | divided_by: servings | round | money
    endif
    assign onetime_serving = current_variant.price | times: 1.0 | divided_by: servings | round | money
  endif

  assign has_saving = false

  if has_plan
    comment
      The compare-at on the allocation is what the plan discounts against. When
      the plan carries none, the variant's own price is the next best anchor —
      it is what the same tub costs without the membership.
    endcomment
    if plan_compare <= plan_price
      assign plan_compare = current_variant.price
    endif

    if plan_compare > plan_price
      assign has_saving = true
      assign saving_amount = plan_compare | minus: plan_price
      if plan_percent > 0
        assign saving_percent = plan_percent | round
      else
        assign saving_percent = saving_amount | times: 100.0 | divided_by: plan_compare | round
      endif
    endif
  endif

  comment
    The sticky bar's note. It used to take the card's subline, which is the
    wrong string for it: the bar has room for one qualifier and the saving is
    the one worth carrying up there.
  endcomment
  assign save_label = ''
  if has_saving
    assign save_label = 'Save ' | append: saving_percent | append: '%'
  endif

  assign default_choice = block.settings.default_choice | default: 'member'
  assign show_onetime = block.settings.show_onetime

  assign member_selected = false
  assign onetime_selected = false
  if default_choice == 'member' and has_plan
    assign member_selected = true
  elsif default_choice == 'onetime' and show_onetime
    assign onetime_selected = true
  endif

  assign gift_numbers = '1,2,3,4,5,6' | split: ','
  assign gift_count = 0
  for gift_number in gift_numbers
    assign gift_key = 'gift' | append: gift_number | append: '_title'
    if block.settings[gift_key] != blank
      assign gift_count = gift_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
-%}

<div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-offer" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {%- if request.design_mode and has_plan == false -%}
    <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__editor-note">
      <strong>No membership card is showing.</strong>
      {%- if block.settings.selling_plan_id == blank -%}
        Set Selling Plan ID to the membership plan you want sold here.
      {%- else -%}
        “{{ block.settings.selling_plan_id }}” does not match a selling plan the selected variant can be bought on.
        {%- if current_variant.selling_plan_allocations.size > 0 -%}
          Plans available on this variant:
          <ul>
            {%- for allocation in current_variant.selling_plan_allocations -%}
              <li>{{ allocation.selling_plan.id }} — {{ allocation.selling_plan.name }}</li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- else -%}
          This variant carries no selling plans at all.
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if block.settings.group_label != blank -%}
    <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-label">{{ block.settings.group_label }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div
    class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offers"
    data-cwc-offers
    {% if default_choice == 'none' %}
      data-cwc-no-autoselect
    {% endif %}
  >
    {%- if has_plan -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The promo strip is the card's own header rather than a banner above it,
        so the claim belongs to the offer it qualifies. Card and strip are one
        box here — the strip is inside the card's border instead of pulling up
        against it, which is what lets the card carry a heavier outline than the
        simple offer's without the two rules disagreeing at the corners.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <label
        class="
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-card
          {% if member_selected %}cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer--selected{% endif %}
        "
        data-cwc-offer
        data-cwc-offer-auto
        data-cwc-offer-plan="{{ plan_id }}"
        data-cwc-offer-quantity="1"
        data-cwc-offer-variant="{{ current_variant.id }}"
        data-cwc-offer-name="{{ block.settings.member_label | default: 'Subscribe & Save' | escape }}"
        data-cwc-offer-sub="{{ save_label | escape }}"
      >
        <input
          type="radio"
          name="cwc_supply_{{ section_id }}"
          class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-input"
          value="{{ block.id }}-{{ plan_id }}"
          {% if member_selected %}
            checked
          {% endif %}
        >

        {% if block.settings.promo_text != blank %}
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-promo">{{ block.settings.promo_text }}</span>
        {% endif %}

        {%- comment -%}
          The radio belongs to the head row, not to the card.

          Held outside it — one column for the dot and another for everything
          else — the perks and the gift panel start where the title starts and
          the card reads as one indented block. In the row, the dot marks the
          choice and the argument beneath it runs the full width of the card,
          which is the shape the design asks for.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-inner">
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-head">
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-heading">
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>

              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-heading-text">
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-title">
                  {{ block.settings.member_label | default: 'Subscribe & Save' }}
                </span>

                {% if block.settings.member_sublabel != blank %}
                  <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-subline">
                    {{- block.settings.member_sublabel -}}
                  </span>
                {% endif %}
              </span>
            </span>

            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-price">
              {%- comment -%}
                Charged and struck on one line, rate under it. The two prices
                are the comparison and belong beside each other; the rate is a
                different unit and reads as a footnote to both.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-price-row">
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-now" data-cwc-offer-now>{{ plan_price | money }}</span>
                {% if has_saving %}
                  <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-was" data-cwc-offer-was>{{ plan_compare | money }}</span>
                {% endif %}
              </span>
              {%- comment -%}
                The figure and its unit are separate elements because the
                script rewrites the figure on every variant change and would
                take "/serving" out with it otherwise. The line hides rather
                than disappears for the same reason: a product with no
                servings set has nothing to say here, and a variant that does
                has to be able to bring it back.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <span
                class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-serving"
                data-cwc-offer-serving-line
                {% if member_serving == blank %}
                  hidden
                {% endif %}
              >
                <span data-cwc-offer-serving>{{ member_serving }}</span>
                {{- block.settings.serving_suffix | default: '/serving' }}
              </span>
            </span>
          </span>

          {%- comment -%}
            What it costs to stay, under what it costs to join. Hidden rather
              than absent when the plan has no second adjustment, so the script
              can bring it back on a variant whose plan does.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span
            class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-recurring"
            data-cwc-offer-recurring-line
            {% if plan_recurring == 0 %}
              hidden
            {% endif %}
          >
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-recurring-price">
              {{ block.settings.recurring_prefix | default: 'then' }}
              <span data-cwc-offer-recurring>{{ plan_recurring | money }}</span>{{ block.settings.recurring_suffix }}
            </span>
            {% if block.settings.recurring_note != blank %}
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-recurring-note">
                {{- block.settings.recurring_note -}}
              </span>
            {% endif %}
          </span>

          {%- if block.settings.perks != blank -%}
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-perks cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-perks cwc-rte">
              {{- block.settings.perks -}}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            The gifts, as a panel rather than a strip: they are a second offer
            inside the first — a list with its own heading, its own total and
            its own caveat — and a bare row of tiles cannot say when each one
            arrives.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if gift_count > 0 -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The intro sits outside the panel on purpose: it introduces the
              gifts in the card's own voice, and the panel that follows is the
              list. Inside, it would read as a second heading.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {% if block.settings.gifts_intro != blank %}
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gifts-intro">{{ block.settings.gifts_intro }}</span>
            {% endif %}

            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gifts">
              {%- if block.settings.gifts_title != blank or block.settings.gifts_total != blank -%}
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gifts-head">
                  {% if block.settings.gifts_title != blank %}
                    <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gifts-title">{{ block.settings.gifts_title }}</span>
                  {% endif %}
                  {% if block.settings.gifts_total != blank %}
                    <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gifts-total">{{ block.settings.gifts_total }}</span>
                  {% endif %}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}

              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gifts-body">
                {% if block.settings.gifts_note != blank %}
                  <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gifts-note">{{ block.settings.gifts_note }}</span>
                {% endif %}

                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gifts-grid">
                  {%- for gift_number in gift_numbers -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign gift_prefix = 'gift' | append: gift_number | append: '_'
                      assign gift_key = gift_prefix | append: 'title'
                      assign gift_title = block.settings[gift_key]
                      assign gift_key = gift_prefix | append: 'image'
                      assign gift_image = block.settings[gift_key]
                      assign gift_key = gift_prefix | append: 'value'
                      assign gift_value = block.settings[gift_key]
                      assign gift_key = gift_prefix | append: 'when'
                      assign gift_when = block.settings[gift_key]
                    -%}

                    {%- if gift_title != blank -%}
                      <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gift">
                        {% if gift_value != blank %}
                          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gift-value"
                            >FREE
                            <S>{{ gift_value }}</s>

                          </span>
                        {%- endif %}

                        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gift-frame">
                          {% if gift_image != blank %}
                            <img
                              src="{{ gift_image | image_url: width: 160 }}"
                              alt="{{ gift_title | escape }}"
                              width="160"
                              height="160"
                              loading="lazy"
                            >
                          {% endif %}
                        </span>

                        {% if gift_when != blank %}
                          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gift-when">{{ gift_when }}</span>
                        {% endif %}

                        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__gift-title">{{ gift_title }}</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      </label>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_onetime and block.settings.onetime_label != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A button, not a label with a radio in it. The radio belongs to the group
        above, and a real one here would let the browser's own group behaviour
        fight the script over which option is live. The dot is drawn from the
        same class the real card uses, so the two are indistinguishable.

        It carries no data-cwc-offer-* attributes on purpose: the script finds
        the live selection by its class and then reads plan and quantity off it,
        and every one of those coming back empty is exactly right for a one-time
        purchase.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__onetime-card
          cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-onetime
          {% if onetime_selected %}cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer--selected{% endif %}
        "
        data-cwc-onetime
        data-cwc-onetime-card
        data-cwc-onetime-behavior="select_only"
        data-cwc-onetime-label="{{ block.settings.onetime_label | escape }}"
      >
        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-inner">
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-head">
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-heading">
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>

              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-heading-text">
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-title cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-title--sm">
                  {{ block.settings.onetime_label }}
                </span>

                {% if block.settings.onetime_sublabel != blank %}
                  <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-subline">
                    {{- block.settings.onetime_sublabel -}}
                  </span>
                {% endif %}
              </span>
            </span>

            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-price">
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-now" data-cwc-onetime-price>
                {{- current_variant.price | money -}}
              </span>
              <span
                class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__member-serving"
                data-cwc-onetime-serving-line
                {% if onetime_serving == blank %}
                  hidden
                {% endif %}
              >
                <span data-cwc-onetime-serving>{{ onetime_serving }}</span>
                {{- block.settings.serving_suffix | default: '/serving' }}
              </span>
            </span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </button>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
